# Pinning for the Kali archive, as it ships in the installed image.
#
# Same rule as kali.pref.chroot, and it has to be: the installed system keeps
# the Kali source (kali.list.binary), so without this pin the first
# `apt-get install` of anything that exists in both archives - nmap, john,
# hashcat, wireshark, libssl - could be answered from kali-rolling, and a
# trixie system would start turning into Kali one command at a time. tests/
# smoke.sh checks the two files agree on the number, because "they should match"
# is not a rule anyone can see being kept.
#
# Priority 50 is the number that makes "Debian first, Kali for what Debian does
# not carry" true rather than aspirational; apt_preferences(5) documents 50 as
# installable-but-not-preferred, which is also what Debian itself uses for sid
# in a mixed system.
Package: *
Pin: release n=kali-rolling
Pin-Priority: 50
